#NEXUS

[ xu2018c_fig3: Alvarezsaurian time tree. Alvarezsauria (leader line to the stem below its node), Alvarezsauridae and Parvicursorinae (leader lines to open node circles) are kept as internal labels. Two multi-way nodes: Kol, Albertonykus, the Xixianykus-Albinykus pair and Parvicursorinae; and the five parvicursorines, stem entering at Mononykus' height. 19 tips, 2 polytomies (4, 5 children); 3 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Random-sample case (seed 20261122). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=19;
    TAXLABELS
        Tyrannosauroidea
        Aorun
        Haplocheirus
        Xiyunykus
        Tugulusaurus
        Bannykus
        Bonapartenykus
        Patagonykus
        Achillesaurus
        Alvarezsaurus
        Kol
        Albertonykus
        Xixianykus
        Albinykus
        Shuvuuia
        Parvicursor
        Mononykus
        Linhenykus
        Ceratonykus
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE xu2018c_fig3 = [&R] (Tyrannosauroidea,(Aorun,(Haplocheirus,((Xiyunykus,Tugulusaurus),(Bannykus,(Bonapartenykus,(Patagonykus,(Achillesaurus,(Alvarezsaurus,(Kol,Albertonykus,(Xixianykus,Albinykus),(Shuvuuia,Parvicursor,Mononykus,Linhenykus,Ceratonykus)Parvicursorinae))Alvarezsauridae)))))))Alvarezsauria);
END;
